{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuCMgFoxQ2eBmSo776LP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CVbCxzJrteXF2gcHiWQ488","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-881\\docs\\reviews\\wi-881\\010-ADJUDICATE-d90ac64.md","content":"# WI-881 amendment adjudication: 010 at d90ac64\n\nAnchor: `docs/archive/last_approved` (system-requirements.toml at 04956829; low-level-requirements.toml at b3cfae9b; test-cases.toml at 04eaa891). This is read with sitting 009 (`009-ADJUDICATE-b025047.md`). That sitting found the code sound but returned the three rows: SR-238's Rationale recorded D-006's launch-window residual, while the AC, LLR-026's Detail and TC-026's Expected still claimed the case. The lane's answer, `d90ac640`, touches exactly those three cells and nothing else; I confirmed this with `git diff b0250473..HEAD -- docs/requirements docs/test`. Sitting 009 judged everything else against the code (36 passed in `tests/test_session_stdin.py`), and nothing outside these three cells has changed since.\n\n- [MEANING] SR-238 AcceptanceCriteria + Rationale -> AC: at a wall deadline, idle deadline or ANY coordinator interruption, the direct child and every process still in the group or job have ended before the coordinator continues, and past 10 s the coordinator stops with an error naming what survived. Rationale: the argued exclusions -> AC: the interruption arm applies \"once the platform's process creation has returned the child\". Rationale: the same exclusions, PLUS why stopping is SN-006's cannot-proceed case, and the residual it now bounds -> not the same: the guarantee is narrowed to exclude an interruption inside platform process creation, and the AC carries that change, not only the Rationale. BLESSED. The AC and Rationale now agree: the residual the Rationale argues is exactly the window the AC's new clause leaves out. The condition stays observable, with the 10 s line unchanged. The SN-006 sentence answers gate 006's F2 by saying why a stop is the right response and not a supervision fault.\n- [MEANING] LLR-026 Detail -> the bounded tree kill on a deadline or any interruption; the Windows close, hold and terminate order; the 10 s raise; an uncontainable child as a session error -> the same, PLUS: the launch owns the child from when `Popen` returns, an interruption inside `Popen` is outside the kill and can lose a running POSIX child, the interruption arm applies after `Popen` returns the child, and a failure to end or verify the tree raises `TreeNotEnded` while an ordinary launch error still returns the session error -> not the same: a stated ownership boundary, a narrowed interruption arm, and a new error contract. BLESSED: the Detail now states the design boundary where it belongs, and matches `_spawn_session` (which owns from `Popen`'s return), `_end_launch`, `_end_suspended` and `TreeNotEnded`, all as sitting 009 verified. It decomposes SR-238's narrowed AC without merely re-wording it.\n- [MEANING] TC-026 Expected (Method unchanged since sitting 009) -> SR-026's outcome; the bounded descendants end with no grace period; an interruption ends them as a deadline does; the remaining kill conditions -> the same, but with the interruption arm narrowed to the kit-side windows (\"before containment, after the resume, or during I/O setup or the deadline handoff\"), PLUS the `TreeNotEnded` and ordinary-launch-error clauses -> not the same: changed acceptance conditions. BLESSED: each named window now maps to a test the Method names (`test_an_interruption_before_the_job_ends_the_suspended_child`, `..._after_the_resume_ends_the_launching_child` and `..._in_supervision_ends_the_child`), and the `TreeNotEnded` clauses map to the two cleanup tests and the ordinary-launch-error test. The Expected no longer claims the window inside `Popen` that nothing can show.\n\nVERDICT: MEANING rows=3\n\nAftermath: every rung is released and all three rows are blessed. The act re-attests SR-238, LLR-026 and TC-026 in its own commit.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":810,"cache_read_input_tokens":458705,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":810},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a511e73-e906-4589-9f31-ae73f8534ed7","uuid":"16d69d37-8ec6-4cce-925d-1259559a9804","timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:35:29.142Z","request_id":"req_011CfuCMfxDZqzZdJSzRsU6p","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CVbCxzJrteXF2gcHiWQ488":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-881\\docs\\reviews\\wi-881\\010-ADJUDICATE-d90ac64.md","content":"# WI-881 amendment adjudication: 010 at d90ac64\n\nAnchor: `docs/archive/last_approved` (system-requirements.toml at 04956829; low-level-requirements.toml at b3cfae9b; test-cases.toml at 04eaa891). This is read with sitting 009 (`009-ADJUDICATE-b025047.md`). That sitting found the code sound but returned the three rows: SR-238's Rationale recorded D-006's launch-window residual, while the AC, LLR-026's Detail and TC-026's Expected still claimed the case. The lane's answer, `d90ac640`, touches exactly those three cells and nothing else; I confirmed this with `git diff b0250473..HEAD -- docs/requirements docs/test`. Sitting 009 judged everything else against the code (36 passed in `tests/test_session_stdin.py`), and nothing outside these three cells has changed since.\n\n- [MEANING] SR-238 AcceptanceCriteria + Rationale -> AC: at a wall deadline, idle deadline or ANY coordinator interruption, the direct child and every process still in the group or job have ended before the coordinator continues, and past 10 s the coordinator stops with an error naming what survived. Rationale: the argued exclusions -