nd ordinary-launch-error clauses -> not the same: changed acceptance conditions. BLESSED: each named window now maps to a test the Method names (`test_an_interruption_before_the_job_ends_the_suspended_child`, `..._after_the_resume_ends_the_launching_child` and `..._in_supervision_ends_the_child`), and the `TreeNotEnded` clauses map to the two cleanup tests and the ordinary-launch-error test. The Expected no longer claims the window inside `Popen` that nothing can show.\n\nVERDICT: MEANING rows=3\n\nAftermath: every rung is released and all three rows are blessed. The act re-attests SR-238, LLR-026 and TC-026 in its own commit.\n"}}}
